# Engineering

Stack: Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript. Routes live in `app/`, UI in `components/`, synthetic catalog data in `data/archive.ts`, copy in `locales/messages.ts`, persistence and auth in `lib/`.

Before changing framework-specific code (routing, server components, route handlers, metadata, config), read the matching guide in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`. This Next.js version differs from older training data. Heed deprecation notices. `AGENTS.md` is regenerated by `next dev`; do not delete its Next.js block.

- Match the surrounding file’s style. Do not reformat a file you are not changing.
- Keep server-only work in route handlers and `lib/`. Do not import `archive-store` or secrets into client components.
- Add a route only when an existing page or handler cannot carry the change.
- Prefer the installed dependencies. Do not add a package, database, or external service unless the task requires it.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — client component reading the file store
'use client';
import { readStore } from '@/lib/archive-store';

// ✅ GOOD — route handler enforces access, then returns a public DTO
export async function GET() {
  const records = await listPublicDocuments();
  return Response.json(records);
}
```
